{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>In the second year.</b> According to the plain sense — of Jacob's arrival, and it is the fourth year of the famine, for the grain that remained from the plenty and the money that was in their hand sufficed them for three years; in the fourth year they gave their livestock, in the fifth their land, in the sixth their bodies, in the seventh he gave them seed and they sowed, and in the eighth year they gathered grain from the field and the famine ceased." "<b>Is not concealed.</b> Nothing remains for us to conceal from you about it."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:53.008558615Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}